WEBVTT

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.430
Yuito!

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:29.360
It's not only New Himuka. There's
something wrong with Seiran, too!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.110
They're mass-producing a drug
that uses human brains.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:37.820
But there's no way to save
my sister without it.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:44.370
Here are Lieutenant Sumeragi's
brainwaves when using psionics.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:49.920
And this shows the Kunad Gate's status.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.260
Are you sure about this?

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.720
I still can't say for sure, but...

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.060
The Kunad Gate and Yuito's
psionic power are...

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.540
<i>A crime in reality</i>

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:26.830
<i>For Heaven's sake</i>

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.750
<i>Accepts any fake</i>

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.170
<i>And disappears</i>

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.260
<i>Piling the eternity in fantasy</i>

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.800
<i>Won't take it at all</i>

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.880
<i>I get sick</i>

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.800
<i>A girl looking back</i>

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.220
<i>Casts the miracle</i>

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.180
<i>Into the instant world </i>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.060
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.900
<i>Did you lie?</i>

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:53.980
<i>Spit the venom </i>

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.740
<i>I know why</i>

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.330
<i>I've found a game of ecstasy</i>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:04.950
<i>Red Criminal gets life</i>

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.410
<i>I've never been in love</i>

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:13.250
<i>Don't know when I started</i>
<i>getting sick of this world</i>

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:14.840
<i>We will fly</i>

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.670
<i>Someday I won't be crying</i>

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:22.510
<i>I've been sacrificing myself</i>

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:24.930
<i>Not to hurt anybody</i>

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.030
"The Rebel Yuito"

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:51.080
Plus, that research facility was built
after Karen and I suggested it to Seiran.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:52.130
Huh?

00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.790
I take it Alice is there.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:58.970
Yes. She's still in Other form.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:06.390
We knew the facility would be misused,
but we convinced Seiran to build it.

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:09.640
It was all to save Alice.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.270
You think me foolish?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:14.690
What the hell is wrong with this country?!

00:03:14.690 --> 00:03:17.070
Human experiments in Suoh.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.450
And in Seiran, research on Others
by using human brains.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:25.370
That's why we must take action.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.330
Major General Fubuki,
have you come up with a strategy yet?

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.540
Nagi saw Naomi's metamorphosis.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:38.510
That memory was likely extracted
so it could be studied.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.800
During personality rehabilitation...

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.180
...his memories were stolen?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:46.810
Once I have Nagi's memory data,

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.850
I'll use Arahabaki to transfer
those images to the entire nation.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.690
I've been authorized to enter
Arahabaki's control layer.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:58.860
All right.

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.070
Where is Nagi's memory data?

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.700
They extract memories
that could cause brain damage.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:10.250
That data's in there?

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:13.580
That's where Nagi underwent
personality rehabilitation.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.460
It should be there.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.710
Nagi might still be there, too.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:20.760
He just might be.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.880
You don't have to do this, Hanabi.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:26.550
I know.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:32.100
But if my dad and uncle
really do know something...

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:34.100
I'm in the same boat as you.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:39.860
I was able to disrupt the security system.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:43.190
Did the data Major General Fubuki
provided work?

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:45.200
Yeah, like a charm.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.910
Okay.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:51.240
We're going in.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.800
So Alice is here, too, Fubuki.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:04.470
Arashi, Major General Karen
wants to see you.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.890
He wants Kasane's
entire platoon there, too.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:14.730
I received a report from
the research facility.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.690
You deliberately let
Yuito's platoon escape.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.400
I already told you.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.990
Seiran and I don't necessarily
seek the same thing.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:27.910
You want to turn metamorphosed
individuals back to human form.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:30.950
And Seiran wants to
use Others as weapons.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.790
Research on both is underway.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:34.040
That's right.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.540
Who knows what Seiran hardliners
will do if we make a wrong move?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:42.500
Next time, think more carefully
before you act.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:46.420
Can that facility really help Naomi?

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.510
She's been refusing
to take that drug ever since.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:52.060
Well, I'm not surprised.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.480
No one would take that if
they had any other choice.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:06:01.650
Nevertheless, there is nowhere
more capable of saving Naomi.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:06.440
So she has to keep taking that drug,
even if you have to force her?

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.120
I'm sure he'll do just that.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.410
Is that all you have to say?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.080
No, there's one more thing.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:19.870
We learned something new
about the Kunad Gate.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.880
I think it might interest you,
too, Kasane.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:37.810
Mom! Hurry! This way!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.140
--Yuito, be careful. Don't stand there.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:42.060
--Hurry up!
--Yuito, be careful. Don't stand there.

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:47.860
Ever since he was a kid, he'd never
listen once he made up his mind.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:51.490
How will I make him listen now?

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:53.950
He must. He's a Sumeragi.

00:06:56.370 --> 00:06:59.250
It's me. I'm heading back now.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.750
Summon Lieutenant Sumeragi to HQ.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.000
Yes, sir!

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:10.760
What is it?

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:14.050
Sir, I can't get through
to Lieutenant Sumeragi.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:17.470
I tried comms and brain talk.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.560
Where is the lieutenant now?

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.980
Unclear. He's off duty
and nowhere to be found.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.690
Find him. I'll grant you access
to the surveillance system.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.820
Yes, sir!

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.950
What is going on?

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:31.990
I see.

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.280
A new security plan for Arahabaki.

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:43.080
Where could they be
storing data around here?

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:47.090
It doesn't even look like
a research facility.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:50.800
We'll have to search
every nook and cranny.

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.100
I'll buy you some time. You guys go, now!

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.810
Nagi.

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:00.730
He sacrificed himself for us.

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:05.060
We had no other choice at the time.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.230
We have to help him.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:10.690
You always were one
to think of others, Yuito.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:17.870
I thought you might come back.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.160
After all...

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.870
...we're best friends.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.000
Nagi.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.970
Major General Fubuki, please come with us.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:43.440
Chief Sumeragi wants to see you.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.400
He seems different this time.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:55.110
Has he undergone even more
potent personality rehabilitation?

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:56.410
But...

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:58.990
Personality rehabilitation?

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:03.370
You who defy the great nation of New
Himuka needs to be rehabilitated!

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:04.710
Nagi! Don't!

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.510
Yuito!

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:24.930
Everyone okay?!

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:30.270
Yuito!

00:09:41.490 --> 00:09:45.290
Not again! If I blackout here...

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:54.760
Yuito!

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.010
Don't move, rebel scum!

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:05.480
Or shall I make him an example
of what happens to traitors?

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:24.540
So the link between the Kunad Gate and
Yuito's psionic power has been proven.

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:31.880
Then what Yuito said 50 years
from now is true.

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.300
So then Yuito...

00:10:35.550 --> 00:10:39.220
Our only choice is to kill him?

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:42.640
Well? Say something, Kasane!

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.470
What's the point?

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.390
We'll be the judge of that!

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:51.350
You only think about yourself!

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:56.740
You've been stuck up and
antisocial ever since you enlisted!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:01.570
But you're a quick thinker who
always sees what needs to be done.

00:11:01.570 --> 00:11:04.740
I'll give you that much.

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.120
That's right.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.290
You're a force to be reckoned with.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:12.460
That's why we've stuck with you.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.750
So have a little more faith in us!

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.550
Let's hear what's on your mind!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:23.800
We want to know
what it is you're holding in.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:26.010
What's the point, you ask?

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:29.480
The point is you have something
on your mind, so say it.

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:33.360
Out with it. We have a right to know.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:38.190
That's right. We're all on
the same team, aren't we?

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.660
Forgive me.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.030
So you've no intention of telling us?!

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.540
N-No!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:53.380
I doubt I could explain it very well.
That's why I said it was pointless.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:12:00.130
That is my way of saying... I'm sorry.

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:02.220
Th-That's what you meant?

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.300
Then why didn't you say so?!

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.550
Forgive me.

00:12:06.550 --> 00:12:12.060
I'm sorry I gave you all the wrong idea
by not opening up. That's why--

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:15.230
Y-You think we don't know that?!

00:12:15.230 --> 00:12:18.980
All right, enough, you two.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:20.690
So now what?

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.450
The world will end if we don't kill Yuito.

00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:27.780
I believe that's true.

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:31.660
I can feel it in the Kunad Gate.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:37.090
Do you deny seeing it when it had grown
large enough to consume the world?

00:12:37.090 --> 00:12:42.720
That's what Karen said to me.
He knew I had traveled to the future.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.050
And now the link between
Yuito and the Kunad Gate

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:49.010
is supposedly scientifically proven.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:52.560
But it's all circumstantial evidence.
Nevertheless...

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:57.310
So you think killing Yuito
is the only solution?

00:12:57.310 --> 00:13:02.070
But deep down, you wonder
whether there is another way?

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:04.650
And the same with Naomi?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:08.580
That makes sense since we
can't trust Karen or Seiran.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.450
And that research facility is bad news.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.370
Let's figure out whether
we can save Naomi.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:18.290
We can do that and
everything else together.

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:23.130
That's right. We're comrades-in-arms
willing to die for each other.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:24.050
I'm sorry.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:26.680
Wrong again, Kasane.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:27.680
Huh?

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:33.020
Isn't there something else you
should say in situations like this?

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:40.400
Oh, um... everyone...

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:43.570
Thank you.

00:13:56.000 --> 00:13:58.330
Fubuki did?

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:02.000
I see. Continue the pursuit.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:06.420
I'll be back.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:19.650
Yuito? That scared you, didn't it?

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.940
The tests are over.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:25.070
Now, look at your mother.

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:31.700
Don't cry. Everything's okay now.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.240
Mom!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:43.590
Test subject, Lieutenant Yuito Sumeragi.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:51.590
Age 16. Registration number SY567369.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:55.180
AKA, Savior of our Nation.

00:15:00.440 --> 00:15:03.150
Use your psionics.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:06.780
Use them to remove your restraints.

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.120
The psionics control system
is operating normally.

00:15:16.120 --> 00:15:18.750
Commencing treatment.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.370
H-Hang on!

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:24.210
What is this place? Who are you?

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:40.020
You don't remember me?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:41.350
What?

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:44.940
We've met here a number of times.

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:48.610
Seventeen times 11 years ago,
to be precise.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.200
I've met you before?

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:55.950
It's only natural not to recall
someone that one met at a hospital.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:16:00.710
But I will check the test
subject's state for the record.

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:05.340
Do you remember being hospitalized here?

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.840
The test subject exhibits
a lapse in memory.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:12.550
E-Enough about that!
Where are my friends?!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:18.260
The cause seems to lie in the decreased
binding rate of his psionic hormone.

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:22.890
According to our data, his sudden
manifestation of psionic power

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:28.940
11 years ago was a process that differed
from the usual dud modification.

00:16:28.940 --> 00:16:30.530
A dud?

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:35.200
It seems the subject also has
no memory of being a dud.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:36.030
Huh?

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:41.540
I believe damage is accumulating in
the brain with each use of psionics.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:45.790
The subject also likely suffers
from sudden memory lapses.

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:49.420
What are you talking about?
Was I once a dud?

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:52.220
There is only a 0.5% success rate

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:56.180
in our dosing tests
on citizens born as duds.

00:16:56.180 --> 00:17:02.730
Only an extremely small number
manifested power as an acquired ability.

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:06.520
And only 0.2% of these
acquired psionics users

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:10.440
have been identified as having powers
exceeding an average level.

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:14.950
However, the test subject's case
is a first.

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:19.120
In an effort to establish
countermeasures for future duds,

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:23.460
we should dissect the subject
and collect his brain data.

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:26.040
I shall seek dissection approval.

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.550
Yuito!

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:32.880
Hanabi!

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.550
Major General?! What are you doing here?

00:17:38.550 --> 00:17:40.510
The program I gave to your platoon

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:45.690
is able to transfer video feeds from
the facility's surveillance cameras.

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.810
We're saved.

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:49.980
And what about Nagi?!

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:54.030
I don't know. And we couldn't
find his memory data.

00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.870
Yuito! You're all right.

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:02.370
What a relief.

00:18:02.370 --> 00:18:05.500
Sorry, everyone. And thanks.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:09.250
You're always saving my behind.

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:14.670
We better hurry. The OSF
already knows we're here.

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:17.380
They'll be here shortly.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:21.970
Major General Fubuki told me
about the escape route.

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:25.100
Others... are gathering.

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:30.810
Get out of here, now.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.400
I'll hold them off.

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.480
But...

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.570
Take this.

00:18:35.570 --> 00:18:37.030
What is it?

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.360
The pass for Arahabaki.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:42.620
It will output a one-time passcode.

00:18:44.330 --> 00:18:46.620
Now, hurry. Go!

00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:49.330
I'm a Septentrion, after all.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:51.670
I'm more than capable of taking them on.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.750
Major General...

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:56.460
We better hurry, Yuito.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.050
Be careful!

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:12.730
Karen!

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:18.320
Yuito. At last, you, too,
reveal yourself for the rebel you are.

00:19:18.320 --> 00:19:20.240
What?

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:22.070
Don't tell me...?!

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:27.830
The nation's savior, Yuito Sumeragi,
is facing arrest for the crime of treason.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:32.130
Lieutenant Sumeragi and his platoon
infiltrated a government facility.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:36.050
There, they were seen sabotaging--

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.340
I don't understand.

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:41.630
You won't be able to set foot in Suoh now.

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:45.220
How about it, Yuito? Join us in Seiran.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:49.730
Seiran will welcome you as comrades.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:54.400
Join those who use human brains
to conduct research on Others?!

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:58.490
New Himuka is conducting experiments
on morphing humans into Others

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:01.400
to develop more powerful psionics.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:04.740
And Suoh plays a central role
in New Himuka's efforts.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.080
Both sides have done wrong.

00:20:06.080 --> 00:20:07.660
Both sides have gone mad!

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:09.450
Then what will you do?

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:12.960
Flee to Togetsu and their
religious pretensions?

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:15.040
They're a theocratic autonomous zone.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:20.090
They might welcome those seen
as criminals outside their borders.

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:21.340
Togetsu?

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:25.350
Yeah, New Himuka wouldn't dare
make a move against them.

00:20:25.350 --> 00:20:27.850
It's an independent city.

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:32.140
Karen, did you come here
just to tell us that?

00:20:32.140 --> 00:20:34.480
I had some other business.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:37.520
Take this if you're going to Togetsu.

00:20:39.070 --> 00:20:40.490
That's...!

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:43.280
You'll need it if you want to survive,

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:47.740
even if it does contain
human blood and brains.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:54.460
Without this, you'll eventually lose
your memory and ability to use psionics.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:57.920
It will delay the inevitable.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:01.340
You may not like it, but you've no choice.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.970
Karen!

00:21:09.970 --> 00:21:12.810
Hurry! They're coming after you!

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:37.920
Karen.

00:21:46.510 --> 00:21:50.220
I suppose they'll make
their move anytime now.

00:22:01.270 --> 00:22:04.400
Holding things in again, are we?

00:22:04.400 --> 00:22:08.030
Didn't I tell you we'll do this together?

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:09.950
Kyoka.

00:22:09.950 --> 00:22:13.410
Is it about Yuito? Or is it Naomi?

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.000
It's both, isn't it?

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:20.420
Is it really a good idea to stick
with Karen and remain in Seiran?

00:22:20.420 --> 00:22:22.130
I was thinking...

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:24.760
...what if we went to Togetsu?

00:24:09.190 --> 00:24:11.950
"Togetsu"
